changetrack-ng (0.7.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Reconcile deleted files in tracked directories against metadata sidecar
    and stage/record removal across Git, SVN, Mercurial, Fossil, and RCS.
  * Bidirectional file type transition handling (file <-> symlink, trackable <->
    non-trackable).
  * Propagate --debug and --trace flags from CLI subcommands to Runner and run_cmd.
  * Drop-in configuration permission audit: check all loaded config files for
    0640 permissions when secrets are present.
  * Config parser strips inline '#' and ';' comments and supports full-line ';'
    comments.
  * Test suite platform safety: probe symlink creation capability and use core
    IO::Uncompress::Gunzip.
  * Add loaded_files() accessor to ChangeTrack::Config and remove() to VCS backends.

 -- Christopher Cashell <topher@zyp.org>  Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

changetrack-ng (0.7.0) unstable; urgency=high

  * Security hardening release consolidated from a multi-tool security review
    (see SECURITY-REVIEW.md / SECURITY-PLAN.md / SECURITY-IMPL-LOG.md).
  * Explicit TLS verification (verify_SSL=1) on the webhook and otlp notifiers;
    previously relied on the HTTP::Tiny default, unverified on the Perl 5.20 floor.
  * Redact credentials (URI userinfo and token-like params) in the --debug command
    trace, the --debug config dump, webhook failure warnings, and Git/Fossil/
    Mercurial push-failure warnings.
  * Strip CR/LF/NUL from OTLP headers; add a sendmail '--' terminator and strip
    CR/LF from mail headers; skip relative PATH entries when locating sendmail.
  * Reject '..' segments in track paths and assert whole-repo mirror paths stay
    within output_dir.
  * Atomic metadata save via File::Temp (O_EXCL, mode 0600); open the lock file
    with O_NOFOLLOW and drop the bare /tmp fallback; revert re-checks the target
    is a regular file before chmod/chown.
  * New command_timeout global config key (default 120s, 0 = unlimited) bounds
    every external command so a hung command cannot hang a scheduled run.
  * run_cmd drains stdout/stderr to EOF (no truncation) and reports signal
    termination; status/diff/log fail loudly on backend errors; notifier failures
    warn and are recorded; a failed metadata save aborts before commit.
  * Add ctime to the metadata fast path; fix RCS colon-encoding collisions; the
    webhook honors max_diff_bytes and suppresses sensitive line counts.
  * Numerous correctness and POD fixes (see CHANGELOG.md).
  * Migration: self-signed TLS endpoints now require insecure=1; RCS archive names
    change for paths containing a literal colon; tracked symlinks re-snapshot once;
    '..' in track paths is now a fatal config error.

 -- Christopher Cashell <topher@zyp.org>  Mon, 29 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000

changetrack-ng (0.6.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * OTel conformance: canonical attribute model on the otlp and file notifiers
    (file.path/name/directory, config_change.type/sensitive/diff, file.mode,
    file.owner.name, file.group.name, file.size, changetrack.files_tracked,
    changetrack.run_duration_ms) and namespaced event names
    (changetrack.file.changed/created/removed, run.heartbeat, run.warning).
  * Add occurred-time vs observed-time distinction: occurred = file mtime
    (timestamp / timeUnixNano), observed = scan start (observed_timestamp /
    observedTimeUnixNano).
  * File notifier now writes one OTel record per event as append-only NDJSON,
    replacing the previous single-object-per-run format.
  * Add config keys (otlp and file notifiers): emit_recipients, max_diff_bytes,
    severity_change, severity_heartbeat, severity_warning.
  * Fix: register the new notifier keys in the config-file parse whitelist so
    setting them no longer aborts config parsing.

 -- Christopher Cashell <topher@zyp.org>  Thu, 25 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000

changetrack-ng (0.6.0) unstable; urgency=high

  * BREAKING: Notifier configuration redesigned. The flat notify= list and all
    [global]-prefixed notifier keys (email_to, email_from, webhook_url,
    webhook_full_diff, otlp_endpoint, otlp_headers, otlp_compression,
    otlp_heartbeat, otlp_full_diff, otlp_resource_attributes, notify_log_path,
    file_heartbeat) are removed. Configure notifiers via [notifier:<type>:<name>]
    subsections; enabled = true|false is required in every section. Multiple
    instances of the same type are supported. Duplicate instance names across all
    loaded files are a fatal parse error.
  * BREAKING: migrate-config subcommand removed.
  * Add drop-in directory support: conf.d/ ([global] only), track.d/ ([track]
    only), notifier.d/ ([notifier:*] only) adjacent to the main config file,
    scanned automatically in sorted order.
  * Add @include, @include-track, @include-notifier directives; directory paths
    process *.conf files in sorted order; visited-paths guard prevents cycles.
  * Add multi-instance notifiers: multiple [notifier:<type>:<name>] sections
    produce independent notifier objects dispatched on every run.
  * Install creates conf.d/, track.d/, notifier.d/ under /etc/changetrack-ng/.
  * Add t/24-config-sections.t, t/25-config-drop-in-dirs.t,
    t/26-config-include-directives.t, t/27-config-cross-file-errors.t.

 -- Christopher Cashell <topher@zyp.org>  Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

changetrack-ng (0.5.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add --system and --user flags for explicit config scope declaration.
    The two flags are mutually exclusive; --user without HOME set exits 64.
  * Add CHANGETRACK_CONFIG environment variable: overrides default config location;
    lower priority than -c/--config, higher than --system/--user scope flags.
  * Source /etc/default/changetrack-ng (Debian) or /etc/sysconfig/changetrack-ng
    (RHEL) from cron script, systemd service, and all package manager hooks.
    Template defaults file installed by make install-hooks.
  * Add DEFAULTSDIR Makefile variable (auto-detected: /etc/default on Debian,
    /etc/sysconfig on RHEL via 'command -v dnf').
  * Add t/23-config-resolution.t: 8-test suite for config resolution priority.

 -- Christopher Cashell <topher@zyp.org>  Thu, 15 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

changetrack-ng (0.5.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add three-tier diagnostic system: --verbose/-v (high-level run structure),
    --debug/-d (external commands + effective config with secrets redacted),
    --trace/-t (per-file disposition for all tracked paths, O(N) output).
    Implication chain: --trace enables --debug; --debug enables --verbose.
    All diagnostic output goes to STDERR; STDOUT stays clean.
  * Add t/22-verbose-debug.t: 42-test suite for the diagnostic tiers.
  * Add PRODUCT.md and CONTRIBUTING.md project documentation files.

